  "title": "South Korea's Re-examination of Missing Person Cases Amid Police Scandal",
  "summary": "South Korea's police will re-examine 310,000 missing person cases after a scandal involving an officer who falsified records to close files on two people who were later found dead. The government has ordered an investigation into the police handling of the cases and plans to reform criminal justice to address systemic issues.",
  "facts": [
