      "title": "Bullet-riddled bodies of two missing SPOs recovered in J-K's Kishtwar",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/j-k-intensifies-search-for-two-missing-spos-in-kishtwar-rushes-forces-126111200079_1.html",
      "description": "Security forces have rushed reinforcement and widened the search for two missing Special Police Officers (SPOs) across the forested upper reaches of Dachhan in Jammu and Kashmir's Kishtwar district for the second consecutive day on Thursday, officials said.\nSpecialised teams equipped with drones and sniffer dogs have been deployed across the forested stretches and difficult mountainous terrain, the officials said.\nBabi Chand, 57, and Rashpal Kumar, 45, both posted with the Special Operations Group (SOG) of the local police at Kiyar village in Dachhan, went missing on Wednesday while travelling from their camp to an Army post at Dharna-Marwah.\nTheir mobile phones were initially reachable but were later switched off, raising concerns among security agencies and prompting to launch an extensive search operation.\nAdditional police and Army personnel have been deployed to intensify the search, with multiple teams fanning out across the vast forested stretches and difficult mountainous .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-12T03:44:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "2 SPOs go missing in J-K's Kishtwar, massive search operation launched",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/2-spos-go-missing-in-j-k-s-kishtwar-massive-search-operation-launched-126111101619_1.html",
      "description": "Two Special Police Officers (SPOs) went missing from the higher reaches of Dachhan in Jammu and Kashmir's Kishtwar district on Wednesday, prompting security forces to launch a massive joint search operation to trace them, officials said.\nThe missing personnel have been identified as Babi Chand (57) and Rashpal Kumar (45), both of whom were posted with the Special Operations Group (SOG) of the local police at their Kiyar village in Dachhan, the officials said.\nThey said the two SPOs were travelling from Kiyar camp to an Army post at Dharna-Marwah when they failed to reach their destination. Their mobile phones were initially reachable but were later switched off, raising concerns about their whereabouts.\nFollowing their disappearance, a massive search operation was launched jointly by the police and the Army's Rashtriya Rifles to locate the missing personnel.\nSecurity teams were deployed in the surrounding areas, including difficult and mountainous forest terrain, to establish their",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-12T02:50:25"
    }
